      "explanation": "A negative exponent takes the reciprocal, and an exponent of \\(1/4\\) means the positive fourth root. Since the base is positive,\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac14\\right)^{-1/4}\n=4^{1/4}\n=\\sqrt{\\sqrt4}\n=\\boxed{\\sqrt2}.\n\\]\nThus the answer is choice E.",
